:: cinema.caro.first-meeting -> @exit
  @place-key cinema
  @auto enter-place
  @priority 500
  @when npc.caro.present and npc.caro.schedule.obligationId == "caro_part_time_cinema"
  @when not npc.caro.met
  @onenter
    @effect relationship caro.rapport 1
    @effect set flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered
  @endonenter

  The attendant behind the ticket counter is trying to restock a display of sweets without letting the queue see how precariously the boxes are balanced.

  She catches one against her hip, looks up, and gives you a quick, victorious smile. "Caro Novak. Welcome to the glamorous side of the film industry."

  You introduce yourself while she straightens the last box. Caro glances towards the programme board, then back to you as if filing your face alongside the week's films.

  @next "Nice save" -> @exit

:: cinema.caro.school-recognition -> @exit
  @place-key cinema
  @auto enter-place
  @priority 500
  @when npc.caro.present and npc.caro.schedule.obligationId == "caro_part_time_cinema"
  @when npc.caro.met and flags.npc.caro.school_encountered and not flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered
  @onenter
    @effect relationship caro.rapport 1
    @effect set flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered
  @endonenter

  The attendant turns from the ticket printer, and you recognise her before the cinema uniform can make the thought seem unlikely.

  "Nurse Caro?"

  Caro closes her eyes for half a second. "Here I'm just Caro. Preferably Caro-who-is-not-about-to-take-anyone's-temperature." She smooths the front of her uniform. "The school pays like it expects gratitude to cover rent. This place pays for the rest."

  Her embarrassment gives way to a crooked smile. "Keep my glamorous double life quiet and I might steer you away from the truly awful films."

  @next "Your secret is safe" -> @exit

:: place.cinema
  @hub cinema

  Backlit posters line the foyer of {{place.name}}. The smell of popcorn drifts from the concession stand while the screens rumble faintly beyond the ticket barrier.
